  "narrative": [
    {
      "type": "description",
      "text": "The press corps fills the briefing room. Cameras flash. The microphones are hot. Nadia Voss sits in the front row, her pen poised over her notebook like a dagger. It is time for the monthly address to the press. The tone you set today will dictate the headlines for the next four weeks."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "character": "nadia_voss",
      "text": "Chancellor. The nation is watching. We have questions about the economy, the border, the reforms. How you answer them today will shape the public's trust. The floor is yours."
    },
    {
      "type": "monologue",
      "text": "The press can be a weapon or a shield. I can attack them, placate them, deflect them, or trust them with the truth. Each path carries its own risks."
    }
  ],
